  "customHelp": "Opening hand: 6 cards.\nMulligan: once, choose any number from 0 to 6; selected cards are returned to the deck, the deck is shuffled, and the same number of cards are drawn.\nMain Deck: exactly 71 cards, maximum 4 copies of any card.\nBangboo: exactly 1 card, kept separate from the Main Deck.\nCurrency: exactly 20 total cards combined between Polychromes and Monochromes; any split is legal.\nStart of game: 6 Main Deck cards enter the Life Pool; 2 Polychromes enter the Wallet face up; the selected Bangboo enters the Bangboo Zone.\nFirst player's first turn: no normal 2-card Main Deck draw.\nEvery turn: draw 1 Polychrome into the Wallet; on all turns after the first player's opening turn, draw 2 Main Deck cards. Tapped cards untap normally at the start of their owner's turn.\nCurrency deckbuilding: Polychromes and Monochromes are separate extra-deck categories. Each individual currency card may be included up to 20 copies. The intended combined maximum is 20 total currency cards. TCG Arena's documented deck ruleset has no cross-category sum validator, so the combined 20 rule cannot be enforced by the native deck-builder configuration alone.",
